{"name":"Aqua Tint","hex":"#e5f1ee","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aqua (user interface)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a graphical user interface, design language and visual theme used in Apple's macOS operating system. It was themed to replicate water, with \"droplet-like\" components and a heavy use of reflective effects and translucency. Its goal was to \"incorporate color, depth, and complex textures into a visually appealing interface\" in macOS applications. At its introduction, Steve Jobs noted that \"... it's liquid, one of the design goals was when you saw it you wanted to lick it\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/Macosxpb.png/330px-Macosxpb.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(user_interface)"},{"title":"Aqua (Chicago)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is an 82-story mixed-use skyscraper in Lakeshore East, downtown Chicago, Illinois. Designed by a team led by Jeanne Gang of Studio Gang Architects, with James Loewenberg of Loewenberg & Associates as the Architect of Record, it includes five levels of parking below ground. The building's eighty-story, 140,000 sq ft (13,000 m2) base is topped by a 82,550 sq ft (7,669 m2) terrace with gardens, gazebos, pools, hot tubs, a walking/running track and a fire pit. Each floor covers approximately 16,000 sq ft (1,500 m2)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Aqua_%28Chicago%29_logo.png/330px-Aqua_%28Chicago%29_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(Chicago)"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone"},{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/66/Dashboard_Ripple.png/250px-Dashboard_Ripple.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/66/Dashboard_Ripple.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/66/Dashboard_Ripple.png/250px-Dashboard_Ripple.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A widget being added to the Dashboard in Mac OS X 10.4. Shown here is the ripple effect.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADashboard_Ripple.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/AM_MacOSX_Panther.png/500px-AM_MacOSX_Panther.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/AM_MacOSX_Panther.png/500px-AM_MacOSX_Panther.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAM_MacOSX_Panther.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Leopard_Desktop.png/500px-Leopard_Desktop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Leopard_Desktop.png/500px-Leopard_Desktop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeopard_Desktop.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg/500px-Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg/1280px-Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg/500px-Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipe